"answer": "Project Zenith is an ambitious initiative launched by Zenith Aerospace Inc. in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole, aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility. The project kicked off on July 15th, with a call for ideas from R&D submitted by July 20th to leverage AI in data visualization. A team expansion added five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. The project reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule with the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, leading to planned UI enhancements in October. A significant milestone was celebrated on October 10th, marking the successful completion of the testing phase. Phase Two progress includes a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report to be shared on November 20th. The project budget was adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration. Additionally, a $15,000 training budget was approved for the coding team and project managers, starting next month. Partnership opportunities with TechInnovate for AI technology are also being explored."
